  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-Uganda Sida Fair Finance 24-27</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For Uganda, extractive industries (specifically mining, oil, and gas) and infrastructure will be the two priority sectors in Uganda. Fair Finance Uganda will add a financial sector advocacy aspect to the current initiatives on natural resource governance, tax justice, and public finance management. The coalition will build the capacity of CSOs to evaluate and monitor the policies and practices of FIs in providing financing and funding that recognizes and respects the social and environmental wellbeing ofthe identified beneficiaries in the extractives industries sector. It will challenge investment and funding policies and practices of FIs and government regulations that continue to exclude millions from accessing quality social services (education and health) in Uganda. The focus will include workers&#x2019; rights and rights of affected communities, especially women and children and promote tax justice as well as transparency and accountability in education and health infrastructure investments.
The Uganda Fair Finance Coalition will conduct capacity building training for CSOs and CBOs on:
-
advocacy and campaigning to influence financial institutions (DFIs/MDBs)

human rights, gender, environmental, social and governance policies
Case studies are planned on transparency and accountability of IFIs (DFIs/MDBs), financing for infrastructure projects in Uganda and extractive industries projects (oil, gold, rare metals)
Fair Finance Uganda consists of: Oxfam in Uganda, Resource Rights Africa, Publish What You Pay (PWYP) Uganda, Seatini, Civic Response on Environment and Development (CRED), Education Advocacy Network, and Centre for Budget and Tax Policy (CBTP).</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib is one of the 17 national affiliates of the Oxfam International Confederation. It started life in 1956 as the Netherlands Organisation for International Assistance (Novib), and joined forces with Oxfam in 1994.  Working together in confederation, the Oxfam affiliates can speak with one clear and compelling voice on issues of global concern: climate change, health and education forall, agriculture, trade, and conflicts and emergencies.  Oxfam established this country office to support local organizations and projects.  Through this local office Oxfam Novib directly contributes towards this project&#x92;s implementation.</narrative>
